---
description: Project coding standards and best practices for VERDEXIS
---

# VERDEXIS Coding Standards

## Code Style
- Write minimal, focused code - only what's needed to solve the requirement
- Use TypeScript for type safety across the stack
- Follow existing project patterns and architecture
- Prioritize readability and maintainability

## Project Structure
- Frontend: React + Vite in /app directory
- Backend: Express + Prisma in /server directory
- Use environment variables for configuration

## Security
- Never expose credentials or sensitive data
- Validate all user inputs
- Follow authentication best practices

## Testing
- Only add tests when explicitly requested
- Use existing test patterns in testsprite_tests/

## Documentation
- Do not create .md files unless explicitly requested

## Deployment
- Always verify code won't break deployment before pushing to git
- Ensure all environment variables are properly configured
- Test build processes before committing
